<DocsPageSubtitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSubtitle>

<Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is3">
    Write Positive Labels
</Heading>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use a short label that describes the selected state, such as "Send me updates" instead of a negative statement. When checks form a related set, introduce them with a visible question or legend while retaining a clear label for every option.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is3">
    Use the Right Selection Control
</Heading>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    The indeterminate state should summarize a mixed group of child values rather than act as a third submitted choice. When users must choose exactly one mutually exclusive option, use a <Anchor To="docs/components/radio">RadioGroup</Anchor> instead.
</DocsPageParagraph>

